{"name":"Log Cabin","hex":"#705a46","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"log cabin","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dwelling made from logs; especially, a small and simple one."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/log_cabin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Log cabin","blocks":[{"text":"A log cabin is a small log house, especially a minimally finished or less architecturally sophisticated structure. Log cabins have an ancient history in Europe, and in North America are often associated with first-generation home building by settlers. Construction with logs was described by the Roman architect Vitruvius Pollio in his architectural treatise De Architectura. He described the log-based dwellings in Pontus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Norskfolkemuseum_1.jpg/330px-Norskfolkemuseum_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Log_cabin","wikidata":"Q695207"},{"title":"Log Cabin (quilt block)","blocks":[{"text":"The Log Cabin quilt block is a North American pieced quilt pattern where narrow strips of fabric surround a central square. Usually, the block is bisected diagonally, with one half using lighter colors than the other half. Sometimes the shading is not diagonal, but in alternating rectangles. Traditionally, the rectangles represent logs in a log cabin, while the central square represents the hearth. Log Cabin blocks have at least three rows of \"logs\", but can have more."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Log_cabin_quilt_-_DPLA_-_711907956a7a5aa0563308cb2f380ad4_%28page_3%29.jpg/330px-Log_cabin_quilt_-_DPLA_-_711907956a7a5aa0563308cb2f380ad4_%28page_3%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Log_Cabin_(quilt_block)","wikidata":"Q127416605"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Gorskii_04654u.jpg/500px-Gorskii_04654u.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Gorskii_04654u.jpg/1280px-Gorskii_04654u.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Gorskii_04654u.jpg/500px-Gorskii_04654u.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A log cabin in Russia, photographed by Sergey Prokudin-Gorsky in 1912","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGorskii_04654u.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Mountain_log_cabin_in_Pyrohiv_2409.JPG/500px-Mountain_log_cabin_in_Pyrohiv_2409.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Mountain_log_cabin_in_Pyrohiv_2409.JPG/500px-Mountain_log_cabin_in_Pyrohiv_2409.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A timber cutter's mountain log cabin at the Museum of Folk Architecture and Life in Pyrohiv, Ukraine","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMountain_log_cabin_in_Pyrohiv_2409.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Nothnagle_Log_House.JPG/250px-Nothnagle_Log_House.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Nothnagle_Log_House.JPG/500px-Nothnagle_Log_House.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Nothnagle_Log_House.JPG/250px-Nothnagle_Log_House.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANothnagle_Log_House.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Abe-Lincoln-Birthplace-2